some product 0 shortages, so it is a little worse than 3.\n- **2**: orders every 3 days, about 1.15 times demand for both products. It saves 4 order fees (about 172) but pays roughly 250 more in storage. Occasional overflow is possible. It is the borderline fourth place.\n- **1**: orders every 2 days at forecast level or below (product 0 about 0.93 times, product 1 about 0.97–1.0). It ignores the 1.046 average, so it has many shortages at 13 each.\n- **5**: orders every 3 days at about 1.3 times demand. At a product 1 arrival the warehouse needs about 163 + 70 + 20 ≈ 253 places, more than 232. So it both overflows and overstocks.\n- **4**: orders every 4 days. At a product 1 arrival it needs about 191 + 63 + 20 ≈ 274 places. Roughly 40 units are lost each cycle, which then causes shortages. That costs about 400 per cycle, more than the order fees it saves.\n- **7**: orders every day, about 27 orders instead of 13. That adds about 600 in order fees, while storage savings are only about 150.\n\n**Result:** the best half is most likely 3, 6, 0 and 2. The least certain call is 2 against 1."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4384, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2313, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4384}, "output_tokens": 10, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-28T22:17:17.622Z", "request_id": "req_011CgVQdcdkbZuriHmXABCW9"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_019mtmy7ovbvTkQchR5LoBwu", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direc